  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great ape public awareness project using video-centered education outreach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to conserve great ape populations in northern Republic of Congo by raising awareness in rural communities using a participatory approach that involves screenings and dissemination of films to ultimately reduce illegal great ape and bushmeat hunting, ritual wildlife killings, habitat destruction and disease transmission. The recipient will reduce great ape and bushmeat hunting and consumption in the departments of Cuvette Ouest,.Cuvette, Sangha, and Likouala through a sustained awareness campaign aimed at eliminating activities that threaten great ape populations; reduce the possibility of future Ebola outbreaks among human populations through an awareness campaign aimed at eliminating activities that increase the risk of disease transmission between great apes and humans; reduce the national demand for great ape and other illegal bushmeat by raising awareness through dissemination of locally produced video to national media outlets and community radio stations, highlighting major issues negatively impacting great apes; increase awareness and acceptance among local communities in Cuvette Ouest, Cuvette, Sangha, and Likouala for the need to develop and consume alternative protein sources; and improve the effectiveness of outreach campaigns using a long-term strategy of evaluation that clearly shows increases in knowledge, and ultimately shows changes of behavior, in target audiences but also informs the need for adaptations of INCEF outreach videos in our ongoing effortgoris.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
